.TH SDL_GDKSuspendComplete 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GDKSuspendComplete \- Callback from the application to let the suspend continue.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_main.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_GDKSuspendComplete(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This should be called in response to an
.BR SDL_EVENT_DID_ENTER_BACKGROUND
event, which can be detected via event watch\[char46] However, do NOT call this function directly from within an event watch callback\[char46] Instead, wait until the app has suppressed all rendering operations, then call this from the application render thread\[char46]
.PP
When using
.BR SDL_Render ,
this should be called after calling
.BR SDL_GDKSuspendRenderer \[char46]
.PP
When using
.BR SDL_GPU ,
this should be called after calling
.BR SDL_GDKSuspendGPU \[char46]
.PP
If you\(aqre writing your own D3D12 renderer, this should be called after calling
.BR ID3D12CommandQueue::SuspendX \[char46]
.PP
This function is only needed for Xbox GDK support; all other platforms will do nothing and set an \(dqunsupported\(dq error message\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function is not thread safe\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_AddEventWatch (3)
